    {
      "id": "31d-Directions-Compounds",
      "sourceSha256": "7b9a6952ed0fb4ed64f28eac334256686a341089228ab1124251235f68011504",
      "testClass": "feature",
      "description": "This tests various combinations of <direction> children. The lyrics for each note describe the compound elements assigned to that note. The first \u2018molto f\u2019 uses <words>molto <words>, i.e., it omits the \u2018xml:space\u2019 attribute. This makes the rendering of the space between \u2018molto\u2019 and \u2018f\u2019 implementation-dependent (and might be thus not rendered). The second \u2018molto f\u2019, together with \u2018meno f\u2019, uses \u2018xml:space=\"preserve\"\u2019. For demonstration purposes, there is no space between the words \u2018bold\u2019 and \u2018italic\u2019. A trailing up-arrow indicates a \u2018placement=\"above\"\u2019 attribute, a down-arrow means \u2018placement=\"below\"\u2019.",
